kind: vulnerability
title: "Cisco ISE: authenticated root command execution CVE-2026-20181 and unauthenticated information disclosure CVE-2026-20190, two independent flaws"
headline: "Cisco fixes two independent ISE flaws: admin-authenticated root command execution and an unauthenticated read of hashed credentials"
summary: "Cisco's advisory of 2026-06-17 covers two independent flaws in Identity Services Engine and ISE-PIC. CVE-2026-20181 (CVSS 9.1) lets an attacker with valid administrative credentials run commands as root on ISE 3.1 to 3.5; CVE-2026-20190 (CVSS 7.5) lets an unauthenticated attacker read sensitive information, including hashed credentials, on ISE 3.4 and 3.5. Cisco says the two do not depend on one another, lists no workaround and is not aware of malicious use."
event_date: 2026-06-17
priority: routine
immediate_action: null
tags:
